      "content": "It is completely understandable that your sense of purpose feels shattered when something so central to your life is gone. When the anchors of your past are gone, it feels like you are adrift in a vast, meaningless ocean. Instead of trying to find a grand \"reason,\" perhaps focus on the smallest, most immediate moments of survival and comfort right now. Small steps, even just getting through the next hour, can become a quiet form of resistance against the void.",
      "source": "target",
